ound the city in  search of one last bodega breakfast  sandwich before the lunch menu goes up  at 11am  a whole bunch of hilarity ensues mostly  involving a perfectly functioning toilet  they find on the street  and a daylight robbery in the shadow of  the brooklyn bridge  and yeah it's all a little weird but  that's broad city for you  finally ilana and abby throw one last  party in part ways for good but  promise to stay in touch regularly over  the phone this finale simultaneously  wraps up the story neatly and  perfectly captures the zany heartwarming  energy that made broad city one of the  best shows of the decade  by the time you reach the end part of  you wants to just flip back to season 1  and start it all over again which is  exactly the mark of a truly great finale  the appropriately named office episode  finale pivots around angela martin's  marriage to salesman turned manager  dwight schrute also features a seriously  meta team  q a panel about well the office  do you find that your life feels  pointless now that nobody's actually  filming you anymore  yes in the iconic show's final moments  the main cast gathers in the office to  spend a final evening together  on paper it's overstuffed even for a  double episode but after nine seasons  it honestly feels like it's not enough  you want every moment to drag on a  little longer because the thought of  your time at dunder mifflin scranton  coming to an end  is well a little bit heartbreaking and  so what if it's a little sappy  finale is a pitch perfect ending for an  outrageous comedy that found its heart  and then some along the way  in terms of highlights everyone loves  the michael scott appearance  but the ending is arguably the best  moment of all  perhaps that's the show's greatest  accomplishment taking a cast of  potentially boring background characters  and bringing them to life while  lampooning the mundanity of 9-5 work  everyone is a bit of a star in the end  and everyone gets just enough of 